Version: 2.0.0
Release Date: 2026-01-14
Codename: Consolidation
Status: Stable
Compatibility: ai-pack 2.x

## Release Notes

This is a major release that consolidates agent tracking on Beads as the single source of truth, removing the deprecated dual-tracking system.

### Breaking Changes
- ❌ **REMOVED:** `agent-status-tracker.py` - Use Beads instead
- ❌ **REMOVED:** `.claude/.agent-status.json` tracking
- ⚠️ **Migration Required:** Use `scripts/migrate-agent-status-to-beads.py`

### New Features
- ✅ **Single source of truth:** Beads only for all task and agent tracking
- ✅ **Agent coordination:** Orchestrator creates Beads tasks when spawning agents
- ✅ **Cross-session persistence:** Agent tasks survive session boundaries
- ✅ **Real-time monitoring:** `/ai-pack agents` command queries Beads
- ✅ **Worker integration:** Engineer/Tester/Reviewer roles update Beads tasks
- ✅ **Git-backed audit trail:** All agent activity tracked in `.beads/issues.jsonl`

### Updated Documentation
- Orchestrator role: Added Section 2.13 (Agent Registration Protocol)
- Orchestrator SKILL: Replaced agent-status-tracker with Beads
- `/ai-pack agents` command: Complete rewrite to query Beads
- Worker roles: Added Beads update instructions
- Coordinator SKILL: Updated to use Beads queries
- Health command: Updated agent status checks

### Migration Path
Projects using agent-status-tracker.py should migrate:
1. Ensure Beads initialized: `bd init`
2. Run migration: `python3 scripts/migrate-agent-status-to-beads.py`
3. Verify: `/ai-pack agents` or `bd list --assignee "Engineer-*"`

See: MIGRATION.md for complete guide

